{title: You'll Be in my Heart}
{artist: Phil Collins}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: Intro}
[F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Come stop your cryin' it will [C]be al[F]right
[F]Just take my hand, [C]hold it [F]tight
[Bb]I will protect you from all around you
[Gm]I will be here, don't you [C]cry
[F]For one so small, you [C]seem so [F]strong
[F]My arms will hold you keep you [C]safe and [F]warm
[Bb]This bond between us, can't be broken
[Gm]I will be here, don't you [C]cry [A]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]You'll be in my [G]heart, Yes, [A]you'll be in my [F#m]heart
From [Bm]this day [G]on, now and for[C]ever [A]more
[D]You'll be in my [G]heart, no [A]matter what they [F#m]say
You'll [Bm]be here in my [G]heart, al[C]ways[A]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Why can't they understand the [C]way we [F]feel?
[F]They just don't trust what they [C]can't ex[F]plain
[Bb]I know we're different but deep inside us
[Gm]We're not that different at [C]all [A]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]You'll be in my [G]heart, [A]you'll be in my [F#m]heart
From [Bm]this day [G]on, now and for[C]ever [A]more
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Don't [Gadd11]listen to [G]them, [Gadd9]what do they [G]know?
We [C]need each other to [Em]have, to hold
[Bm]They'll see in time. I [C]know[A]
When [Gadd11]destiny [G]calls you, you [Gadd9]must be [G]strong
I [C]may not be with you, but you [Em]got to hold on
[Bm]They'll see in time. I [C]know
We'll [D]show them to[A]gether[E]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Cause [E]You'll be in my [A]heart, Believe me, [B]you'll be in my [G#m]heart
From [C#m]this day [A]on, now and for[D]ever [B]more
[E]You'll be in my [A]heart, no [B]matter what they [G#m]say
You'll [C#m]be here in my [A]heart, al[D]ways[B]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Ending}
[A]Always, I'll be [E]with you
I'll be [A]there for you always
Always and [E]always
Just look [A]over your shoulder
Just look [E]over your shoulder
Just look [A]over your shoulder
And I'll be there [E]always
{end_of_verse}
